# Without this the build context is ~150 GB: the repository root carries the
# conda installation (116 GB), a 10 GB tarball, demo imagery and years of run
# outputs. Docker would send all of it to the daemon before the first layer.
# Strategy: exclude everything, then re-include only what the Dockerfile COPYs.

**

!docker/**
!environments/**
!segment-anything-2/gui/**

# ...then take the bulk back out of gui/. Only code, prompts and small assets
# belong in an image; data lives on a mounted volume.
segment-anything-2/gui/Demo/**
segment-anything-2/gui/outputs/**
segment-anything-2/gui/outputs_final/**
segment-anything-2/gui/unlabeled_masks/**
segment-anything-2/gui/envs/**
segment-anything-2/gui/metric3d/**
segment-anything-2/gui/measure/_Mickey_/**
segment-anything-2/gui/measure/custom_outputs/**
segment-anything-2/gui/measure/outputs/**
segment-anything-2/gui/measure/results_*/**
segment-anything-2/gui/DINOSAR_v2/**

# generated, heavy or irrelevant everywhere
**/__pycache__/**
**/*.pyc
**/.git/**
**/*.tar.gz
**/*.zip
**/*.log
**/*.bak*
**/*.whl
**/*.pth
**/*.pt
**/*.pkl
**/*.npz
**/*.npy
**/*.tif
**/*.tiff

# ...except the few small assets the GUI genuinely needs at runtime
!segment-anything-2/gui/marmot.jpg
!segment-anything-2/gui/icons/**
!segment-anything-2/gui/measure/biorag_prompts/**
